# THE REPOSITORY ROOT GITIGNORES A DIRECTORY NAMED `runs`, AND IT SWALLOWED THIS
# ROUTE SILENTLY.
#
# `/.gitignore:27` is `runs/` -- UNANCHORED, so it matches a directory called
# `runs` at ANY depth, not only the repository root's run-log directory (the one
# CLAUDE.md says never to `ls`, ~10k files). This app's run history lives at
# `web/app/(routes)/runs/`, so every file under it was ignored.
#
# WHAT MADE IT DANGEROUS RATHER THAN ANNOYING: `git add` on an ignored path is not
# an error unless you name the path exactly. `git add web/` reports success and
# adds nothing from here, so the screen would have been missing from the commit
# with the working tree looking complete and every gate green. That is this
# repository's signature failure shape -- a step reporting success for work it did
# not do -- arriving in git rather than in the pipeline.
#
# Measured:
#     git check-ignore -v "web/app/(routes)/runs/page.tsx"
#     .gitignore:27:runs/   web/app/(routes)/runs/page.tsx
#
# THE FIX IS HERE AND NOT AT THE ROOT, deliberately. Anchoring the root rule to
# `/runs/` would be correct and is a one-character edit to a file this lane does
# not own -- and it would silently widen what the root ignores for every other
# lane and every future directory. A negation scoped to this directory cannot
# affect anything outside it.
#
# The trailing slash matters: `!runs` would not re-include a DIRECTORY excluded by
# a directory pattern.
!runs/
